{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794389755,"nonce":"CUhYxIvyQumcz0c8eG7+be1tZrc=","title":"Bindings must not pass an HDLL primitive as a function value while Ash's JIT rejects it on threads","message":"On Ash 0.1.17, an HDLL primitive taken as a function value fails when it is\ncalled from a thread made by `sys.thread.Thread.create`, in `--mode jit` and\nin the default hybrid mode:\n\n    compiled worker reached unprepared JIT sentinel for findex N\n\n`--mode interp` and stock HashLink 1.15.0 run the same bytecode correctly.\nCalling the primitive directly, or through a Haxe lambda, works everywhere.\n\n`hxn.Future.then` waits on a helper thread, so a binding that hands\n`Native.future_take_int` to `hxn.Future` as its `take` hits this. The\ncounter fixture did, and now passes `raw -\u003e Native.future_take_int(raw)`.\n\nUntil Ash fixes it, anything that generates HashLink bindings (the\n`hxn.Bind` macro, `hxn gen --emit-haxe`) should emit a lambda around a\nprimitive wherever a function value is needed, never the primitive itself.\n\nReported to the Ash session with a standalone reproduction on 2026-11-11.\nThe reproduction: take `var live:() -\u003e Int = Native.live;` for any\nno-argument primitive, call `live()` inside `Thread.create`, and report the\nresult through `events.runPromised`.","files":null}]}